WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.580
Yeah!

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.080
You think we're getting a new song soon?

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.540
I wonder what kind of song
we're getting next?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.200
--Huh? Hold on, Miu!
--Miu!

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.540
--Miu?
--What happened?

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.040
"Happy☆Jet☆Coaster"

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.040
Food poisoning?

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:12.870
"Happy☆Jet☆Coaster"

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:12.870
Yes.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.700
It seems Jun was the only one who didn't eat
the coffee jelly we put out for them.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.160
She seems to dislike bitter things.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.410
Surely this had to be one of the Wall's Orders.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.290
We're looking into it with the store
who made the jelly at the moment.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.120
How is everyone?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.370
The doctor said they should perk back up
with a little rest, peace, and quiet.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.370
Fortunately their symptoms were light,
so they're headed towards a full recovery.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:38.330
Is that so?

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.410
Thank goodness it wasn't serious.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:44.500
However, this puts us in a bind
with regard to their schedule.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.870
It's one small mercy
that Toda was safe in all of this.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.620
She'll just have to fill the hole
left by the others for now.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.910
We're in a rush.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.790
Lookin' forward to workin' with you!

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.500
After that, I want
tons of treats in our dressing room.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.080
Also those custard kashiwamochi
rice cakes from Azabu.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.080
The croquette lunch set
from Oageya will be fine.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.830
Miss Toda, what's with that getup?

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.080
Oh, Gouda. Good day to you, sir.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.790
Please go and change.
You'll be quite busy today.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:21.700
Oh, but if my health were to get worse,
you wouldn't have any replacement for me.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.450
That's how it is, so...

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.950
Regardless, please go change.
We don't time for this. We have to hurry.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.330
W-Wait! Gouda!

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.500
Yes, yes!
Just leave it to me!

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.500
I'll do a splendid job all by myself!

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.950
Her boundless good cheer
just may save us this time.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.830
You may be right.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.910
I've never seen her be anything
but that cheerful self of hers.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.830
All right!

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:12.120
"5 YEARS AGO"

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.540
I was born with a weak respiratory tract.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.450
Since I was little, it's been
an endless cycle of hospitalizations,

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:59.330
and I was prone to going home early.
At school, I ended up in the nurse's office.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:02.790
I didn't have any friends at school at all.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.200
Jun!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.620
My doctor said it would be difficult
for me to make a full recovery,

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.410
that I was born with this
and it wasn't anyone's fault.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.330
I thought that this was my fate
to spend my life like this.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.870
"YUU MATSUNAGA"
"JUN TODA"

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:46.080
This bed again? It's not even cute.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.750
Hey, Mom. Is this my bed?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.540
Wow, it's so fluffy!

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.750
And it's white, too! How cute!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.000
This bed? Cute?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.450
--Oh, and the sheets smell so good, too!

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.120
--Is this her first time in a hospital?
What a strange girl.
--Oh, and the sheets smell so good, too!

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.750
--Is this her first time in a hospital?
What a strange girl.
--Yuu, stop playing around.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.750
Okay!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.450
None of this is cute.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.410
It's just the usual boring, white bed.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:17.870
Hello, and welcome to today's
Naminami Egg here on FM 73.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.830
I'm Yoshizaka, your host today.
And with me I have...

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:24.540
Filling in for Mya-ko,
it's Jun Toda as your co-host for today!

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.660
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:30.040
I heard that Miyako isn't feeling too well.
Is she okay?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.450
Oh, she's fine!

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.910
It was most likely something she ate.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:37.700
Should I ask what you've been doing
for the last few minutes, Jun?

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.200
Signing autographs!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.450
My manager said that I needed
to get this entire stack done by lunch.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.950
None of the others are doing any signing?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:48.830
--No one knows the answer to that question.
--You know we're live, right?

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:54.700
If anyone wants an autograph, go and participate
in the event we're having at noon!

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.540
Ah, all done!

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.290
Time for lunch.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.830
It's time to go.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.200
After this, we have the mini-concert
in Odaiba at noon.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.660
We have Sato's
fashion magazine interview at 2 PM.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:10.250
At 4 PM, you'll be pitch-hitting
for Fujima's English lesson show.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.500
At 7 PM, you're on a live show
at an amusement park,

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.370
and early tomorrow you'll be
doing a recording at a studio.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.120
M-My lunch!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.830
I'll do my best, everyone!

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.830
I'll really do my best!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.200
Jun!

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.450
Jun Toda!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.290
Yeah.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.620
Your name is so cute!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.410
And the way you spell it in katakana is so cool,
like you're a foreigner or something!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.870
R-Really?

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.000
My name's Yuu! Nice to meet you!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.540
Nice to meet you.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.540
Hey, want to come play with me?

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.370
Huh?

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.410
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.330
We had the same one!

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:17.660
Wow, you really do know everyone here.
That's amazing.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.290
Okay, we're starting!

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:22.000
One, two,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.250
--three...
--This way.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.700
...four, five,

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.750
six, seven...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.950
We can hide really well if we go up here.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.830
...29, 30!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.620
Here I come!

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.000
Are you okay?
Do you want to get a little closer?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.000
Look! Is that Mount Fuji?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.200
So pretty!

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:55.200
Yuu, you look like you're having fun.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.500
Hm?

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:02.870
No, I keep wondering how you always
seem like you're able to have a good time.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.580
You mean you're not having fun, Jun?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.540
I've been thinking...

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:18.000
Because I really can't go to school,
I'm dumb and can't make friends.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:22.870
My meds are hard to deal with,
and I start coughing really quick.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:27.620
I keep thinking that if things will be
like this forever, what am I gonna do?

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:39.500
Well, I think life is like an amusement park.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:43.950
Injections are like a roller coaster.
Medications are like haunted houses!

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.370
You've just gotten to an amusement park.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.950
Having a sad face at one of those
is such a waste.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.700
An amusement park?

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.040
Ah, I found you, Jun!

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.910
Jun!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.250
Are you okay?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.580
Everyone, come quick!

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.370
Jun fell!

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.910
Jun!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.830
Jun?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.040
Well, okay, let's get them out here!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.500
Here's 22/7!

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.000
Everyone!

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.870
My current obsession
is custard kashiwamochi!

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:35.830
I'm sweets-loving 15-year-old Jun Toda!

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:36.660
Huh?

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:38.540
There's only one of them?

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.120
The others aren't feeling well.
They're taking the day off,

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:45.290
so I thought I would fill in today
as all of 22/7 myself!

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.910
What?!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.870
Hey, don't say, "What?"

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.290
Right, Nicole?

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.450
♪ Niconicorunrun, nicorunrun! ♪

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.580
I'm Nicole Saito,
an entertainer who dances with a smile!

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.750
Everything can be quantified
in numerical form,

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:07.330
so I would like to calculate that for you.
I'm Akane Maruyama.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.040
Is it really that strange?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.950
Just where did my cool demeanor go?

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:15.870
Oh, no, here comes Mya-ko,
and right before my self-introduction, too!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.410
She is impersonating all of them.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:21.120
This is great! Keep going!

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.450
Um, I'm Miu Takigawa.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:31.950
And now that we're all warmed up,
let's hit the music!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.870
The fact that you
endorsed our sponsors saved us.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:41.040
I'm relieved to see
that the fans had a great time, too.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:43.910
Whatever, gimme some food... Food...

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.160
Here. Here's a fried chicken lunchbox.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.160
Heck yeah! Fried chicken!

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.950
However, it's time for us to go.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.870
Let's get going!

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.080
Okay, let's do it!

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.160
"KARAOKE"

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.580
"KARAOKE"

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.580
H-Hey, Yuu, this isn't good!

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.120
"KARAOKE"

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.120
It's fine!

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.040
But the nurse was giving us a suspicious look.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.750
If we get back before dusk, we're good!

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.410
But how do we get in?

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:15.410
"TOMOE MATSUNAGA"

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:15.410
♪ If you look around in the crowd ♪

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:19.160
♪ There are some cute girls ♪

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:25.250
♪ Those somber flowers won't realize that ♪

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:28.000
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah ♪

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:31.950
♪ The music playing in the cafeteria ♪

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:35.790
♪ If you space out and give it a listen ♪

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:39.540
♪ You'll find that at some point ♪

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:43.040
♪ Your foot has started to
tap along to the beat ♪

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.000
♪ You can't stop ♪

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.160
♪ This feeling ♪

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.620
♪ Come on, come on, come on,
come on, baby ♪

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.580
♪ Tell my fortune ♪

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.500
♪ This fortune cookie of love ♪

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.950
♪ Your future doesn't look too bad ♪

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:01.870
♪ Hey, hey, hey ♪

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.660
♪ You can say you like me ♪

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:07.370
♪ If you show me your smile ♪

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:11.290
♪ This fortune cookie of the heart ♪

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:15.700
♪ Your fortune for tomorrow
will be better than today's ♪

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:20.580
♪ Hey, hey, hey ♪

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:24.290
♪ You haven't thrown your life away ♪

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:28.290
♪ After this, you'll be surprised
at the miracles that will occur ♪

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:34.540
♪ I have this feeling
that you and I will meet again ♪

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.200
Yes, as the leader,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:50.000
I'm always thinking
about ways to advance as a group.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.620
By Reika Sato.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.040
Hey, Jun! Hurry and clean this mess up!

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.410
Smack, smack!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.080
Stop!

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.950
Next is Fujima's English lesson show.
You'll be a substitute host!

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.750
Smack, smack, smack!

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:06.080
That interview already ended!

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.700
Hey, guys!

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.370
Welcome, welcome! Yay!

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.160
Is your name Jun
because you were born in June?

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.580
Jun?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:15.870
Jun-June?

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.700
You were born in May!

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.080
Jun-June.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.700
As always, thanks!

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.160
Thank you!

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.870
Next!

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.290
I want to run more!

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.160
That's the flavor of youth!

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.660
Okay, cut! Thank you for your hard work!

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:31.910
Thank you very mu--

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.250
Next!

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:47.870
Okay.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.620
I-It's finally over.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.120
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.080
The only things left
are an interview and a meeting.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.250
And...

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.450
More autograph boards.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.040
Bathroom...

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:10.700
This really seems hard on her.

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.540
It definitely does.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:31.080
Thank you so much for this.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:34.370
It seems that Jun's cheered up
a bit more this time around.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:38.500
Yes, it seems like she's gotten more positive.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:46.950
Dear Yuu, thank you for always playing
with me while I was here in the hospital.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:52.660
Because of you, the time I spent
in the hospital was so much fun.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.160
From now on, I'm going
to take a page from your book

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:58.580
and try to have fun no matter what.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:02.160
Ever since you got your own room,

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:05.500
we haven't seen each other,
and I've been kinda lonely.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:08.620
But after I get discharged,
I swear I'll come visit you.

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.620
We'll always, always be friends forever.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.660
"PRIVATE ROOM"

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.660
So let's play again together some day!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.200
From Jun.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:49.290
"EXAMINATION ROOM 1"

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:55.910
--Jun?
--Jun?

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:41.500
I... I...

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.410
I should've been the one to died.

00:17:56.410 --> 00:18:02.750
Instead of me, who's so negative,
she was the one that should've lived.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:08.620
Yuu was always so happy
and positive every day.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:14.620
She made friends with me,
even though I'm so boring.

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:19.410
God, it isn't too late.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:23.200
So please, exchange my life for hers.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.450
She's been crying nonstop for three days now.

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:46.580
She won't come out of her room or eat.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.370
Luckily, her coughing has calmed down.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.870
I think it's okay to leave her alone now.

00:18:57.910 --> 00:18:59.540
It's a full recovery.

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:02.120
I haven't been able to find any irregularities.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.910
We'll have to keep an eye
on it for a bit, but...

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.000
...since she's made a full recovery,
she should be fine.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.620
Yes, you heard me right, Mom!

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:18.500
We're at the hospital right now.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.540
Yes, a full recovery!

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.450
I talked to Jun about it already.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.040
--They didn't even say how strange it was.
--Let's all just meet at the park.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.450
--They didn't even say how strange it was.
--Roger that!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.950
That was a turning point for me.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:47.500
The illness that had tormented my lungs
for the last ten years was gone completely.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:53.040
The doctor said that it would
have been okay to cry every night, but...

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:58.290
I shouldn't give into those feelings.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:02.290
Because it was as if I'd received Yuu's life.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:04.660
It was that sort of event.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:19.330
Life is... an amusement park!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:21.290
"MISS JUN TODA, YOU HAVE BEEN SELECTED
AS A MEMBER IN OUR NEW PROJECT."

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:26.500
I did it!

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:29.000
I'm done with work for today!

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:33.410
Congratulations.
We hope you'll work just as hard tomorrow.

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.410
Sleep...

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.250
We've prepared a nap room for you.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:41.200
She really does have amazing stamina
to get all of that done.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:46.330
Just where in that tiny body of hers
does she hide that much vitality?

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.250
Wait.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.160
Why are we all together?

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:02.000
No real reason. Pure happenstance.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:06.000
--My quick recovery is a gift
thanks to my professionalism.
--Now, now. I think it's better to be relaxed,
so let's do that.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:09.200
I'm different from the rest of you,
who were just snoring away.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.700
Yeah, yeah, whatever, Elizabeth.
You're amazing.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:12.750
Excuse me?

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.040
--Just who is Elizabeth?
--Now, now, now...

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:19.200
Calm down, everyone.
We're still recovering, right?

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.620
Jun.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:26.200
Ah, Jun!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.450
I missed you guys!

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:31.080
Jun, did something happen?

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.040
I can finally rest.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.910
Wow, she's letting it all hang out.

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:37.450
But more importantly, Jun,
I heard you on the radio!

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:39.080
You were amazing!

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.910
I was laughing before I knew it.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:43.000
I've come to see you in a new light.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.870
The staff were singing your praises, too.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.910
Thank you, Jun.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.950
Jun...

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:53.580
Thank you so much.
I know it must have been a lot.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.870
Oh, for the love of...

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:03.040
You guys have no clue what I went through!

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:05.330
It was so...

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:07.500
...so, so...

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:11.580
...so...

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:13.250
...much fun!

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:17.540
--It was fun? What the heck?
--Geez.

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:07.040
"SEPTEMBER 22nd
HOLD A SOLO LIVE SHOW
FOR 3,000 PEOPLE"

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:09.950
"Episode 8: Dreaming Robot"

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:11.950
"Episode 8: Dreaming Robot"

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:11.950
"Dreaming Robot."
